 "db_defects_reported_not_patched": [
  "DEF-0171-1  ilogic's byte0 match [[0,8,11]] is over-fitted to destination r0; byte0 = (dst<<4)|0x0b, HARDWARE-PROVEN 15/15 observable registers. ilogic and b_alu10_lof/b_alu10_loe are ONE instruction.",
  "DEF-0171-2  no length rule for byte0 == 0x31, so G17P's own native bfloat ALU does not tokenize at all; bf_alu's match (byte0==0x11, byte+1==0x02) and bf_fma_dst.fmt's enum {2,4} do not describe what G17P emits (byte0 0x31, byte+1 0x00).",
  "DEF-0171-3  ibfe.sign_ext (byte+6 bit1) is NOT the sign control -- dense-inert in BOTH the signed and unsigned compiler anchors. The signed/unsigned difference rides on srcC_flags byte+9 bit0 (INFERRED; byte+9 not swept here).",
  "DEF-0171-4  ilogic.outmod / b_alu10_*.outmod byte+7 bit7 is a SOURCE-READ control, not the 'output/store flag' db.json names: with it clear the LUT still evaluates and the destination is still written, but both sources read as ZERO (k_nand writes 0xFFFFFFFF = ~(0&0)).",
  "DEF-0171-5  fspecial_est.subop == 0x0f in G17P's precise rsqrt lowering, a value absent from db.json's enum {9: rcp, 11: rsqrt, 13: sqrt}."
 ],
